  "result": "Fixed. Arguments containing `#` now complete correctly.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py` uses `shlex`, which treats `#` as a comment start by default. Everything from the `#` onward was dropped from the words being completed.\n\n**Fix:** I set `lex.commenters = \"\"` so `#` is treated as an ordinary character.\n\nI also added a regression test, `test_split_arg_string_hash`, in `tests/test_shell_completion.py`. I added an \"Unreleased\" entry to `CHANGES.md` as well. All 59 tests in `tests/test_shell_completion.py` pass.",
